              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MCCOMBSS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this even more simple by using precooked roasted chicken. I thought the 15 oz jar of Alfredo wouldn’t be enough but it was perfect. Didn’t change anything else. So quick and easy and delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-23T14:26:11.829Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Whisper Fisher"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I will make this again, it was very good. Only thing I would change for next time is to use a bit more sauce. My pasta wasn't dry at all though, i just personally would like to add more. I also added shredded Parmesan cheese and mixed it throughout, then I added graded Parmesan cheese to the pasta (I did not mix the graded cheese). Then i put the pasta in the oven (on 400 degrees) for about 7 minutes just allowing the cheese to melt. I think the extra cheese added more flavor to the pasta.",
            "datePublished": "2017-02-05T22:20:09.110Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paula"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I must admit I was prepared to not like this due to the addition of vegetables. Whoever heard of putting mixed vegetables in Alfredo sauce?! But I forged ahead. I cut the recipe in half since I was serving only my husband and myself, and I used rotisserie chicken breast I had in the freezer. Oddly enough, my only complaint is that I ended up using more of the jarred Alfredo sauce and milk because the sauce was a little dry. Surprisingly, the vegetables weren’t off-putting at all. I can see this being a great way to get veggies in those picky kiddos, plus it’s really fast and quick to fix.",
            "datePublished": "2023-03-29T22:52:08.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "David"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I cubed two raw skinless boneless chicken breast halves and cooked them in a wok. Just two of us so I only boiled 5 ounces pasta and only 5 ounces frozen vegetables When chicken was cooked I added the rest of the ingredients and simmered for about 15 minutes until the vegetables were tender crisp. Both of us like it, it's a keeper. Next time I might use cooked rotini and mix it in the wok with the rest of the ingredients.",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-07T00:47:34.510Z"
          },
          {
